notify loop for any managers after the failing one AND 500ing the rep's ping request even though the ping and violation were already committed. Fixed by broadening the catch to `(WebPushException, requests.exceptions.RequestException)`, re-reviewed clean. Three Minor findings shipped as known-acceptable: a TOCTOU race on the at-most-one-open-violation invariant (no DB-level partial unique index; fast-follow), `_is_within_work_hours` not explicitly normalizing to UTC (safe today since `recorded_at` always arrives UTC-aware via the DB round-trip), and no dedicated two-tenant isolation test for the two new endpoint families (code traced correct by the final reviewer, coverage gap only). 234/234 tests passing, ruff clean. This completes Phase 6 (violations & alerts) in full. Next: plan Phase 7 (manager web dashboard).
